From 38634855493e22b493bd304338a34cdb4ae9984d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:16:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: one bottom bar look, every icon from the Plait
 design guide

- PlaitBars: every bottom bar (library tabs, photo viewer, editor tabs,
  editor tool bar) on surfaceContainerLow, 80 dp, no divider. Sections
  are the design guide's nav items (icon in a 64 x 32 accent pill, 12 sp
  label); actions are 40 dp tonal tiles, the one main action (apply)
  solid primary. The system navigation bar continues the bar's colour
- Icons: only the design guide's (plait-design icons.txt -> ps_*.xml,
  copied by plait-os scripts/gallery-icons.py): the Gallery's own icon
  vectors, the editor's bitmap undo/redo, menu marker, add, compare and
  overflow icons, and the video player's play/pause/replay are replaced;
  the old icon files are removed
- Tools grid tiles are TonalTiles (primaryContainer, 12 dp corners)
- versionCode 40059

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
